{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls","id":385184,"title":"Dark Eras Hunter Chapter: Doubting Souls","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-29T09:42:42-08:00","id":385184,"title":"Dark Eras Hunter Chapter: Doubting Souls","content":"Popping in to mention that if you're curious about Doubting Souls the Hunter chapter for Dark Eras, the full unedited text of the supplement is available on the Dark Eras Kickstarter page. The new compacts are the Scarlet Watch and Les Voyageurs. Matt and I will be around to answer your questions if you have any. Hope you dig it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T10:22:13-08:00","id":385243,"title":"","content":"I have only had the chance to speed read through the chapter, but I have to say that it looks like a really compelling setting for a Hunter game, and in my opinion it is by far the strongest part of the entire book. I really like the Scarlet Watch in particular. You might want to include the TV series 'Salem' among the list of Inspirations, along with the third film in the Ginger Snaps trilogy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Have you seen him? </i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1000-mistere","name":"MisterE","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1000_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T10:33:41-08:00","id":385269,"title":"","content":"the Scarlet Watch are awesome. AWESOME. Did something happened to the founder families so they no longer exist? or are they still around, in one form or another? Also, is it just me or that those guys sound like a former conspiracy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T10:46:05-08:00","id":385284,"title":"","content":"How can I read the beta of the book ( or even just chapters )? I do not see the link on Kickstarter page... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T10:46:23-08:00","id":385285,"title":"","content":"I'm thrilled you like the chapter and will pass that along to Matt, too. So here's the GREAT thing about this Kickstarter. If you love the material, make your voice heard and comment on the KS! We can expand the chapter or add a new era...it's totally up to you and your vote counts! WOO!<br /> <br /> Otherwise, how else can we reveal more mysteries? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T10:53:44-08:00","id":385290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=385284#post385284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can I read the beta of the book ( or even just chapters )? I do not see the link on Kickstarter page... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's right under the Demon: the Descent blurb. The forums are cutting off my links.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T11:45:25-08:00","id":385352,"title":"","content":"Overall I liked it. I had big concerns since ignorance and paranoia are parts of the Hunter cannon that I think are too easy to overdo; but this struck the perfect balance I think. Plenty of both, but it also showed intelligent Hunters with a fair amount of diversity in goals and methods.<br /> <br /> The intelligent actions of the various Conspiracies to the black death was a highlight in my mind. It's great to see hunters Conspiracies being large enough to influence big events without being the secret masters of history. I personally believe that Cherion didn't create the black plauge - devastating economies is bad for the bottom line, but creating bioweapons like that sounds the kind of think they could do (and that almost no Supernaturals could) so it was nice to see the implication that they had the ability, even if I think they're innocent.<br /> <br /> The Canites being behind the scenes shadowy manipulators was a big suprise, but after consideration I like it. The paranoia of vampire blood in communion wine is pure Canite, and while the modern group being socially influential seems laughable - I have no trouble imagining that the Canites of centuries past had a completely different set of strengths and weaknesses. <hr /><br /> That said I do have some criticisms too:<br /> <br /> The first sidebar. The God Machine Chronicles makes it very clear that humans in the WoD think differently to real world humans; hence how in the real world most people believe in ghosts which don't exist, and in the WoD no one believes in Ghosts, which are common and visible. This contradicts that \u2013 it would be better to address the issue directly and say that the contradiction is intentional to match real history.<br /> <br /> The Malleus Maleficarum (the Conspiracy, not the book) was curiously absent outside one sidebar in the section the Hammer Swings. IMO that's an <b>enormous </b>omission \u2013 as the Core book says the book called \u201cMalleus Maleficarum\u201d was declared heretical and the MM is responsible for punishing heresy. What were they doing all that time?<br /> <br /> Tiny quibble: the sentence \u201cMost of the group\u2019s members were on the front lines of several skirmishes between vampires and the undying\u2019s cults\u201d seems strange given that in modern days at most a third of the Ascending Ones (and probably a lot less) are ever on the front lines. Now while I admit the older AO could be more hunter focused, I think the mysticism and trade sides have great potential in historial games. <hr /><br /> Onto the new groups:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Scarlet Watch</b><br /> <br /> I really like this group. The idea of random people forced together, uncovering the legacy that binds them, and fulfilling and ancient duty. Firstly it's really cool and secondly it's a great justification for having an odd group of PCs with wildly different backstories. I would suggest adding details on what they lore and Endowments they lost, so that players might recover it.<br /> <br /> That said I didn't grock their founding. They felt betrayed by the Church, and so formed an alliance against vampires... how does that work? They also started working with the Malleus Maleficarum pretty quickly after that.<br /> <br /> I'm also unsure how the Salem era Watch retains a hyperfocus on vampires. Given the dissconnect between the old watch and the modern watch \u2013 and the modern watch's focus on self-defense / mutual-defence I would expect a more pragmatic \u201cI hunt whoever's threatening me\u201d. Vampires might be explicit in their contract, but if so I'd expect more to be done with the disconnect between the vigil they believe in and the vigil they're contractually obliged to follow.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Les Voyageurs</b><br /> <br /> I wasn't as keen on this group, since hunters and fur traders are quite similar to the Bear Lodge. More worryingly, they just don't make sense. They explicitly don't have a backstory, they don't have any particular reason to want to exterminate werewolves \u2013 they don't even have any particular reason to want to sell werewolf pelts instead of beaver pelts. Given the high morality rate the payoff would have to be huge, along the lines of \u201cone pelt, then retirement\u201d and that's not the case.<br /> <br /> Trappers, hunters and the fur trade are a natural place for PCs to hold their vigil, but this just didn't feel like a plausible organisation.<br /> <br /> <br /> I was also disappointed to see the lack of a native group, preferably a Conspiracy. I liked the native stuff in this chapter and would have liked to see them as hunters in their own right rather than just allies or members of European organisations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 01-29-2015, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T11:47:24-08:00","id":385353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=385269#post385269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or are they still around, in one form or another?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think that's up to you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=385269#post385269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, is it just me or that those guys sound like a former conspiracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just you.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T11:53:36-08:00","id":385396,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback, both positive and negative. Many of the criticisms we know we'll receive are partly due to word count restrictions for this chapter. This is considerably smaller than a supplement, being only a chapter, and we jammed as much as possible within the constraints we were given.<br /> <br /> The idea for the way this book intersects with Kickstarter is relatively new. If fans like the core of this chapter (or any other) and vote/comment to see more, we can expand further for this setting or for another one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T01:09:12-08:00","id":386060,"title":"","content":"I really enjoy the setting, and especially like that it feels like all the Conspiracies are bumping into each other a whole bunch. <i>Hunter</i> has a bad habit of making every group feel like they exist in individual vacuums, so making things feel sloppy is perfect. My only complaint is the lack of a Native American compact, which I feel might do something stronger with the space currently used for Les Voyageurs. <br /> <br /> Does anyone know if there are nWoD stats for flintlocks anywhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T05:07:40-08:00","id":386179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=386060#post386060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know if there are nWoD stats for flintlocks anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, in <i>Armory</i>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T08:59:24-08:00","id":386366,"title":"","content":"I was a little sceptical of the idea behind this Dark Era. I just found it too clich\u00e9d and predictable. But I like it. Playing a hunter in a time and place gripped by witch-hunting hysteria and paranoia is a much different experience than the modern Vigil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T10:38:20-08:00","id":386445,"title":"","content":"It's my favorite era, and has all my favorite conspiracies. I particularly like the possibility of hunter versus hunter in-fighting, which was always something you could do in modern nights but there was less reason for it. I really like the new compacts as well, the Voyageurs are a new fave and the Docendo are great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-30-2015, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T23:01:27-08:00","id":387108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=385352#post385352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was also disappointed to see the lack of a native group, preferably a Conspiracy. I liked the native stuff in this chapter and would have liked to see them as hunters in their own right rather than just allies or members of European organisations.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can justify this somewhat with the Great Dying killing enough scores of Natives where the normal Hunters are still picking up the pieces as it where but overall, you're right. It is quite a glaring omission considering the time scale goes with the Last of the Mohicans extremely well (not to mention the British/French using natives as pawns in their games).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T05:54:29-08:00","id":387256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=387108#post387108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can justify this somewhat with the Great Dying killing enough scores of Natives where the normal Hunters are still picking up the pieces as it where but overall, you're right. It is quite a glaring omission considering the time scale goes with the Last of the Mohicans extremely well (not to mention the British/French using natives as pawns in their games).<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you wish to play a Native, you can use the Les Voyageurs compact to do so which, in part, is the reason why it was created. We did not create a Native-specific compact because there was no possible way for us to do it correctly within this chapter. Our Dark Eras chapter was focused on a specific region and theme, and anything else you see is because we wanted to include as many playable options as space would allow.<br /> <br /> Throughout history, there are many Native tribes with different beliefs, cultures, and attitudes. Applying that to the WoD on top of an already complex era of history isn't something any of us take lightly. If we had a full supplement, then we might consider it. Even then, compacts and conspiracies aren't formed around race.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T09:15:31-08:00","id":387447,"title":"","content":"Actually, I think that for a compact/conspiracy based around the Native Americans could have been filled using a sidebar about the localLes Myst\u00e8res (without the voodoo theme, of course). They are pun cultural group who focus about all kinds of shamans and witch doctors, after all, and it felt a little weird that the other &quot;specialist&quot; groups got a sidebar and they didn't.<br /> <br /> Talking about the sidebars, that reminded me how much I liked the one about the Cainte Heresy. It changed a lot the way I pictured them- from a group of fanatics who can barely work together into a real conspiracy who can manipulate the church to hunt for vampires. That was really cool, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T09:20:17-08:00","id":387449,"title":"","content":"You do however have compacts tied to both faiths and nationalities, VASCU is part of the American government, and to a slightly lesser extent VALKARIE is as well. So a compact tied to a specific tribe or a specific native faith has precedent. It wouldn't even be a move away from the region and theme - since Les Voyageurs hunt far inland from coastal Massachusetts and are too isolated to participate or be much affected by mass hysteria or mass anything.<br /> <br /> The only issue is providing background on the tribe itself - you can assume that VASCU players are familiar with the FBI - but links to non-WoD sources should suffice for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T11:03:19-08:00","id":387491,"title":"","content":"well, of course that I would have want a group tied up to a specific tribe/ faith. The more the merrier, as far as I'm concerned. I'm just saying that in case that space was the problem, that would have been a way to address it without wasting too much word count or messing up too much by using inaccurate data. Maybe adding such group could be a stretch goal of some kind or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T12:00:08-08:00","id":387541,"title":"","content":"I missed this post the first time around.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=387447#post387447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I think that for a compact/conspiracy based around the Native Americans could have been filled using a sidebar about the localLes Myst\u00e8res (without the voodoo theme, of course). They are pun cultural group who focus about all kinds of shamans and witch doctors, after all, and it felt a little weird that the other &quot;specialist&quot; groups got a sidebar and they didn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really a fan of this - precisely because it is a pan cultural group. It feels a little unfair to say that Christians get two dedicated organisations plus dedicated membership in the Ascending Ones, and the non-Anglican Knights of St George; but Native Americans only get membership in a generic group.<br /> <br /> That's not to say they I have a problem with Les Mysteriis (Ok, I think their fight with werewolves would be much more interesting if it was doctrinal at it's core). Just that I don't think they can &quot;fill the niche&quot;. And I do think it's a niche that should be filled, native Americans make a great <i>other </i>for European Hunters be suspicious of, yet ultimately require help from to deal with a they don't know about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=387447#post387447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking about the sidebars, that reminded me how much I liked the one about the Cainte Heresy. It changed a lot the way I pictured them- from a group of fanatics who can barely work together into a real conspiracy who can manipulate the church to hunt for vampires. That was really cool, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's so different from the way they're portrayed in Night Stalkers that I came to the conclusion that they're a very very different organisation in Salem times. An actual Conspiracy rather than a large, old, magic using Compact.<br /> <br /> Which makes perfect sense. Vampires are sedentry creatures who acumilate power. Canites are mobile drifters who avoid ties (nice contrast). But as technology advances the advantage goes to the Vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T15:06:09-08:00","id":388981,"title":"","content":"Like I've said, I'll be more then happy to get a native compact/ conspiracy of hunters- but if there are limitations of space and knowledge, one should find a way to work in those limitations.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I agrre that it shows that the Cainte has changed with the passage of time- but still, the idea that once they were united enough to do something like that is awesome, if only because it makes you think more about the nature of their sources.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I really hope that Hunter would get more support in the book, either by expanding the existing material or adding some new Eras (like the French Revolution/ Reign of Terror, for example). I'm an Hunter follower for a reason, and I want it to be as awesome as possible!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T16:54:28-08:00","id":389121,"title":"","content":"Someone gave me an idea last night and even if I don't get to run the dark era I'm going to have a hunt for the hidden library of the Docendo Discimus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T17:06:29-08:00","id":389132,"title":"","content":"I'm happy that folks are digging what we did with the Heresy.<br /> <br /> Now, this chapter is focused on a very specific location and while we did manage to offer up some information about what Hunters are up to beyond the borders of the region we're focused on, our word count was primarily focused on a small region.<br /> <br /> If I was going to focus on the same Era, but a different location, I'd explore other Compacts and Conspiracies than we did in this chapter. Monica and I were very focused on some specific themes and some pretty epic events for the characters in the area.<br /> <br /> -MMM","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Owner/Editor - FlamesRising.com","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T01:10:11-08:00","id":389533,"title":"","content":"You know, it's possible this was covered, I just gave the hunter section a cursory look, but I was thinking that the Cheiron Group really wouldn't fair well in Salem. <br /> , <br /> A group looking for third nipples is going to find werewolf hands, tentacle tongues, and bee guns, especially since according to Compacts and Conspiracies Cheiron has witch informants it pays with thaumatech, so if the witch hunters find a witch in salem with thaumatech they'd definitely start looking for others....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T07:59:03-08:00","id":396375,"title":"","content":"thankfully we can fix the eurocentricisim by voting in the next stretch goal for an expansion that covers the native american hunters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T16:01:47-08:00","id":396878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=389533#post389533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You know, it's possible this was covered, I just gave the hunter section a cursory look, but I was thinking that the Cheiron Group really wouldn't fair well in Salem.<br /> ,<br /> A group looking for third nipples is going to find werewolf hands, tentacle tongues, and bee guns, especially since according to Compacts and Conspiracies Cheiron has witch informants it pays with thaumatech, so if the witch hunters find a witch in salem with thaumatech they'd definitely start looking for others....</div> </div> </div> </div>We added Boston as a location and mentioned that Cheiron Group's iteration in the time period was connected to a shipping company. Boston isn't that far from Salem and is connected to the witch trials, so we felt it was a good extrapolation to ensure CG was covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T16:06:17-08:00","id":396882,"title":"","content":"I will be personally offended if Native Hunters lose the next poll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T04:25:18-08:00","id":397353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=396878#post396878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We added Boston as a location and mentioned that Cheiron Group's iteration in the time period was connected to a shipping company. Boston isn't that far from Salem and is connected to the witch trials, so we felt it was a good extrapolation to ensure CG was covered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must say I liked the bits about Cheiron in the book. It gives us some more information about their past. Now, we can say that the medical and Greek themes are a real part of Cheiron's nature, and not just a cover up for their modern incarnation (sure, that was what I've always thought, but it is nice to get some further support)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T11:20:09-08:00","id":397822,"title":"","content":"Hype Mode fully engaged, picked the best possible era","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Didn't anyone ever tell you not to bring claws to a gun fight?</span></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3786-leicsfox","name":"LeicsFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3786_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T02:25:03-08:00","id":400124,"title":"","content":"Correct me if I'm mistaken - but with the Knights of Saint George and their Shadow Court - the claim that they have any kind of ecumenical authority via the <i>Church of England </i>would be met with contempt by any self-respecting Salem Puritan, wouldn't it? I mean that IS pretty much the exact reason their fore-bearers LEFT ENGLAND, right? As far as Separatist Puritans are concerned, the Church of England is steeped in &quot;Papacy&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mean it's not as bad as a Malleus hunter letting anyone know about their faith - but my point is it isn't a system of religious authority the Puritans recognize - and that was kind of a big deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-10-2015, 05:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T02:26:05-08:00","id":400126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=396882#post396882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will be personally offended if Native Hunters lose the next poll.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's got my vote, but if Elizabethan Changelings win, I can't say I'll be too upset.<br /> <br /> I am curious about some of the indigenous horrors that got name dropped in the chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-10-2015, 05:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T02:38:11-08:00","id":400134,"title":"","content":"Caught a mistake - page 168 refers to Canon Episcopi as being written in 900 BCE, instead of 900 CE","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T05:46:54-08:00","id":400195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=400124#post400124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I'm mistaken - but with the Knights of Saint George and their Shadow Court - the claim that they have any kind of ecumenical authority via the <i>Church of England </i>would be met with contempt by any self-respecting Salem Puritan, wouldn't it? I mean that IS pretty much the exact reason their fore-bearers LEFT ENGLAND, right? As far as Separatist Puritans are concerned, the Church of England is steeped in &quot;Papacy&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mean it's not as bad as a Malleus hunter letting anyone know about their faith - but my point is it isn't a system of religious authority the Puritans recognize - and that was kind of a big deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is true that the Knights of Saint George have a different faith than the Puritans. In this Era, not every Hunter was Puritan nor did Salem Village/Salem/Boston/etc. have a homogeneous population, either. We (Matt and I) feel that this aspect of the game allows for great conflict at the table and was part of our design. That said, the Knights of Saint George are operating in secret, so only Hunters know this Court exists. Hunters have to decide what's more important to them. The Vigil? Or their faith? As the chapter title suggests, Doubting Souls isn't just about the witch trials, it's the conflict Hunters feel hunting in an Era of uncertainty. The Knights of Saint George are part of that theme, and while they'd likely get a frosty reception from the local populace and a few Hunters from the region, most Hunters understand that despite their differences the one thing they share in common is the Vigil. Religious conflict can be an asset to your chronicle, but can also be difficult for players with strong faith. Should you decide to zero in on this aspect of the Era, we recommend approaching it carefully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T15:15:21-08:00","id":412143,"title":"","content":"so I was reading the preview a bit before going to sleep, and I've thought if someone has an idea about how the two compacts which are only mentioned (the Divine Artificer and the Silent Imperative) should be developed? (and if there are more such compacts which I've missed.. damn, this is a big book!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T18:35:16-08:00","id":412290,"title":"","content":"So, now that the chance of details on noneuropean people has been killed off, can we get a full supliment on First Nations hunters covering all of North America? Or, does this mean that we should just pretend that being white is the best chance for a group to get anything written about them, and White Wolf has more implications than previously thought?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1481-obviouspword","name":"ObviousPword","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T19:48:17-08:00","id":412351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ObviousPword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=412290#post412290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, now that the chance of details on noneuropean people has been killed off, can we get a full supliment on First Nations hunters covering all of North America? Or, does this mean that we should just pretend that being white is the best chance for a group to get anything written about them, and White Wolf has more implications than previously thought?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering CWoD awful history of racial stereotyping and Orientalism in their &quot;foreing culture&quot; books, what you're seeing is actually the NWoD playing it safe by comparison. They's said time and time again, they want that kind of material handled by writers from the cultures in question themselves, or living in or from the detailed locals. That said, there has been and continues to be non-Western groups and settings detailed, and many of the signature characters are non-white, so while I'd like to continue to see a wider cultural lens as well, I'd watch myself before throwing around accusations of racism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T19:57:33-08:00","id":412359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=412351#post412351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering CWoD awful history of racial stereotyping and Orientalism in their &quot;foreing culture&quot; books, what you're seeing is actually the NWoD playing it safe by comparison. They's said time and time again, they want that kind of material handled by writers from the cultures in question themselves, or living in or from the detailed locals. That said, there has been and continues to be non-Western groups and settings detailed, and many of the signature characters are non-white, so while I'd like to continue to see a wider cultural lens as well, I'd watch myself before throwing around accusations of racism.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh man. My bad! Let's just pretend that there are absolutely no cultures beyond european ones and be very cagey about addressing any of them. This is MUCH better than actually spending any amount of time doing research or hiring people with first hand experience! I'm sure glad that there's no one reading these books who might be FROM these cultures or WANT to see anything about them. Hahaha. Good thing that's not true. Well, let's write a whole lot more about european countries and eurocentric views of post colonial America! What? Natives? Those don't exist, you're being silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1481-obviouspword","name":"ObviousPword","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T20:03:43-08:00","id":412364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ObviousPword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=412359#post412359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh man. My bad! Let's just pretend that there are absolutely no cultures beyond european ones and be very cagey about addressing any of them. This is MUCH better than actually spending any amount of time doing research or hiring people with first hand experience! I'm sure glad that there's no one reading these books who might be FROM these cultures or WANT to see anything about them. Hahaha. Good thing that's not true. Well, let's write a whole lot more about european countries and eurocentric views of post colonial America! What? Natives? Those don't exist, you're being silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll take &quot;we won't do it until we're sure we don't fuck it up&quot; over oWoD's blatantly disgusting racism any day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T20:17:11-08:00","id":412374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ObviousPword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=412359#post412359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh man. My bad! Let's just pretend that there are absolutely no cultures beyond european ones and be very cagey about addressing any of them. This is MUCH better than actually spending any amount of time doing research or hiring people with first hand experience! I'm sure glad that there's no one reading these books who might be FROM these cultures or WANT to see anything about them. Hahaha. Good thing that's not true. Well, let's write a whole lot more about european countries and eurocentric views of post colonial America! What? Natives? Those don't exist, you're being silly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know Tokyo is one of the signature cities for Second Edition Mage right? And we're getting Ottoman Demon in Dark Eras? And in all liklihood Three Kingdoms Changeling &amp; Geist? And Aztec Skinchangers? And the Maori feature centrally in the New Zealand Geist setting? And there's the entire fucking game of Mummy the Curse, which pretty much openly says there aren't any originally white PCs? And the Ascending Ones in Hunter are based on the Abbasid myth of the Hashashins (and they later wrote up the Al al-Jabal as the historically accurate take on the same originating group)? And the most well known VtR signature character isn't white? And there's an entire Thai Buddhist Covenant written up in Ancient Bloodlines? And Indian Bloodlines?<br /> <br /> They're walking a lot more carefully than the CWoD that would have published a whole book of racist super-stereotype powers by now - but they're not ignoring anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T20:32:59-08:00","id":412387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=412374#post412374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You know Tokyo is one of the signature cities for Second Edition Mage right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some clarity. Tokyo is Second Edition's signature city <i>period. </i>Every gameline is getting it as it's updated, Rose and Dave are working out a Demon incarnation, and it's even appearing in Hurt Locker. And none of this is touching on the vast number of cities from around the world that has gotten looked at, or is planned on.<br /> <br /> As for the overall diverse look, yeah, they aren't diving headlong into it like oWoD did, but considering oWoD tripped over hundreds of bad portrayals, the cautious approach is fine by me. That said, write what you know is still a major rule, and Onyx Path is kind of centrally based in 'The West'. Between the two, Onyx Path is handling it as best they can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T00:04:56-08:00","id":412494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=412387#post412387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some clarity. Tokyo is Second Edition's signature city <i>period. </i>Every gameline is getting it as it's updated, <b>Rose and Dave are working out a Demon incarnation</b>, and it's even appearing in Hurt Locker. And none of this is touching on the vast number of cities from around the world that has gotten looked at, or is planned on.</div> </div> </div> </div>When did this get confirmed? And what would it be showing up in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T00:14:29-08:00","id":412496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=412351#post412351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering CWoD awful history of racial stereotyping and Orientalism in their &quot;foreing culture&quot; books, what you're seeing is actually the NWoD playing it safe by comparison. They's said time and time again, they want that kind of material handled by writers from the cultures in question themselves, or living in or from the detailed locals. That said, there has been and continues to be non-Western groups and settings detailed, and many of the signature characters are non-white, so while I'd like to continue to see a wider cultural lens as well, I'd watch myself before throwing around accusations of racism.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand ObviousPword does bring up a good point. The lack of real focus on native americans is kind of blatently racist, especially in a time period where they are around. On the other hand, white-wolf has written rather racists stuff in the past, gypsies being a great example. What I would like to see is Pword's book idea, of native hunters from across the americas being detailed, and perhaps also some native australians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T00:39:29-08:00","id":412517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=412494#post412494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When did this get confirmed? And what would it be showing up in?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not confirmed in a book, but both David and Rose have mentioned in various threads that they're looking for a place to tackle the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T10:35:01-08:00","id":412931,"title":"","content":"Not extremely happy with Tokyo being the signature city of 2E, but I'm sure many are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T11:28:40-08:00","id":412957,"title":"","content":"While I think ObviousPword was needlessly hostile, rude and ignorant of the support for different ethnicities in WoD 2e I do think that, while getting a member of the culture in question to be the author is obviously the best solution, when the choice is between getting somebody else to write and not writing at all Onyx Path should get that someone else to write. Erasure is worse than misrepresentation.<br /> <br /> That said there's other options that someone ignorant of Native American culture could use for Native American Hunters. Just make it clear that this group is in no way meant to be a realistic portrayal of Native Americans and avoid basing it on bad stereotypes. It's not like, e.g. the Knights of St. George have <i>any</i> resemblance to the Anglican church; something purely fictional like the Knights, Cheireon or AKD, that just happens to exist in North America and thus have a prominently Native American membership is an option.<br /> <br /> (Though personally, I'm metaphorically voting for for a group that does resemble one of the actual Native American nations/faiths/something. Purely fictional groups like the Knights or AKD are cool, but I don't feel there's a conspicuous gap for a purely fictional Conspiracy like there is for something like the the Union that a regular Native American hunter might join after taking up the vigil)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 02-20-2015, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T17:02:47-08:00","id":413388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=412931#post412931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not extremely happy with Tokyo being the signature city of 2E, but I'm sure many are.</div> </div> </div> </div>It stand blatantly in the face of the complaint put forth,at any rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T21:17:53-08:00","id":416130,"title":"","content":"OK, since a change of topic would probably be a good thing at this point, and I've finally gotten around to reading the chapter, let's change topics and talk about some errors of misrepresentation actually present:<br /> <br /> Perhaps the most egregious error is the claim that the Protestant Reformation was <i>directly caused by</i> the Witch Hunts of Europe... In fact, as written in the chapter currently, it is heavily implied as the <i>sole</i> reason for both the Protestant Reformation and Henry VIII forming the Church of England.<br /> <br /> This is ignoring so many factors within the Catholic Church that brought about its own fragmentation and downfall that it's honestly quite astonishing. It's calling a symptom of the disease the cause of the disease, itself. The Catholic Church before the reforms of the (ironically named) Counter-Reformation/Council of Trent routinely engaged in practices that would be seen as naked corruption by modern eyes. The Church openly extorted bribes from the nobility, or coerced massive concessions of land under pain of Excommunication. (And that was basically the equivalent of handing everyone in the world who hated you a license to freely murder you or conquer your lands.) The Church would openly accept money in exchange for making a nobleman the arch-bishop in charge of some of the lands those noblemen likely donated to the church under coercion. In fact, it worked out just fine for them, since, while bishoprics were not hereditary, the money was, and the Church could happily just keep accepting bribes for every successive generation of de facto hereditary lords being given the cloth. They didn't stop at just selling rank, for that matter: They traded holy relics of the saints (things like their finger bones dug up from their graves) for cash. Naturally, there were plenty of con men in the clergy, willing to claim any random pauper's hand was a saint's holy remnants on Earth, and that just having that severed finger would TOTALLY cure you of any disease. If it festers and you get a new disease, that just means you need to buy MORE fingers!<br /> <br /> The Pope rewrote how the heavens work by Papal decree, inventing Purgatory wholecloth, just so that he could charge noblemen bribe money to go to Heaven, instead. That is, overtly trading material wealth for Heaven. You know, the exact thing Simon Magus was supposedly such an evil sorcerer for attempting to perform. These purchases of indulgences were THE single largest listed reason why the Reformation revolted against the Church.<br /> <br /> It's not as though there weren't reformist movements before The Reformation, the Waldesians existed centuries prior, (as did the Lollards and Fratecelli,) which protested the Catholic Church largely as having become materialistic and corrupt and for their efforts, largely <i>were</i> the &quot;pagans&quot; and &quot;witches&quot; that were put to the stake in the earlier witch hunts. (In fact, they likely were the original cause of the widespread belief in witchcraft in the first place, as they helped the church to suppress dissent over their flagrant corruption to declare dissent in league with Satan. That said, the divergence from history on this point for the purpose of setting up ahistoric nWoD factions is an overt divergence from history, so is understandable.) The Franciscans only avoided the same fate by gaining Papal recognition, yet from then on, were a source of constant internal dissent over the materialism of the Church in that era, arguing for ascetic lifestyles for the clergy.<br /> <br /> The reason Martin Luther caused a continent-rending schism when Waldo did not was because the Church of the 15th Century was even more flagrantly corrupt and power-hungry. Look up Pope Alexander VI and the children he had by his Papal mistress, whom he overtly schemed to put into power over Italy through excommunication of all local rivals, giving Church funds to military conquest over Catholic faithful lands, or repeatedly re-marrying his daughter (and killing her husbands or declaring them impotent and annulling their marriage so she could be &quot;reused&quot; as a political token for marriages). Machiavelli wrote <i>The Prince</i> essentially as a <i>resume</i> to the Pope's son, to prove he was ruthless enough to be an adviser to someone as ruthless as the child of the Pope. The name Borgia is synonymous with evil within the Papacy, and is a FAR greater direct cause of the Reformation.<br /> <br /> And it's not like the Papacy itself was alone in critically undermining the moral authority of the Papacy. For much of the Late Renaissance, France overtly <i>owned</i> the Papacy. The Knights Templar were declared heretics and their wealth looted (by the state, not the church) because the King of France could not repay his debts to the bankers of the Church. Oh, and while I'm on the topic, banking was <i>usury</i>, a heresy punishable by death, (the reasons for which are a giant page-long rant in and of itself...) which meant that the Church would kill any business rivals in their pursuit of placing others in debt to them. This was, of course, AFTER the period where the Papacy would excommunicate the would-be successors to the Holy Roman Empire, only to have the Emperor march into the Vatican, execute the Pope, and set up his own puppet Pope who would ensure he would be coronated. Even that was when there weren't TWO people claiming to be Pope, as was often the case, just to help ensure that there was always confusion and an undermining of the legitimacy of the Papacy. (Often rival puppet Popes of France and the Holy Roman Empire.)<br /> <br /> All this is to say there were <i>KIND OF A LOT OF VERY GOOD REASONS WHY PEOPLE WOULD BE UPSET WITH PAPAL RULE</i>, not just one single random thing that happened.<br /> <br /> In fact, the largest, most distinct, most iconic era of the Witch Hunting craze in Europe didn't occur until around 1580, six decades after the Protestant Reformation. Most historians list the Protestant Reformation <i>as a cause of the Witch Hunts</i>, not the other way around.<br /> <br /> Henry VIII simply took advantage of the already massive discontent, and took the chance to use the chaos of the Reformation to break off from the Papacy to get his marriage to a relative of the Holy Roman Emperor (who currently exerted the heaviest influence on the Papacy) annulled.<br /> <br /> In fact, you could pretty much sum up the 16th and 17th Centuries as &quot;The Protestant Reformation happened, and everyone started murdering each other constantly for 200 straight years, to the point of nearly halving the population of what is now Germany, and all the social orders of the Middle Ages fell apart in the bloodbath, and the witch hunts were just another excuse to kill your neighbor before they killed you,&quot; and be done with it. (Although, to add even more confusion to the issue, it's also believed that Lyme Disease, a disease from the New World that caused seizures and was heretofore unknown was treated as demonic possession or evidence of witchcraft, and may have directly led to a lot of the hysteria in Europe that occurred in the decades immediately following some of the earlier round trips to the New World.)<br /> <br /> Speaking in a much broader sense about the whole of the arc of Western Civilization, this was the start of a new era. Following the collapse of the Great Empires in the West, especially Rome, monotheistic religion dominated Europe. This was the collapse of The Church that could hold such a powerful sway over the hearts and minds of populace that they could keep any other true centralized empires from forming, and radically altered how commerce was conducted for 1500 years. This was the collapse of that system into the free-for-all of nations striving for global empires based upon trade and the exploitation of foreign peoples and lands through the slave trade that the Church had previously kept abolished. It was a fundamental change in the social order, and like most fundamental changes in social order, came with a LOT of bloodshed, fear, and paranoia. Again, the witch trials were just a symptom of a MUCH larger movement going on behind the scenes, the grasping paranoia of a populace who was seeing monumental changes to the fundamental structure of their worldview on a scale so massive they couldn't comprehend what was happening, or where it was going, and as such grasped onto easy explanations. That is, rather than the social discord being brought upon by the changing of an epoch, where the social contracts they depended upon were being torn up from beneath their feet, ancestral rights being denied them, their being forced to move from everyone-knows-everyone villages to faceless cities to feed the upcoming Industrial Revolution, or the decay of the feudal societies or church structure that had governed their ancestors lives, or the new diseases ravaging their families being the result of the changes in the world they couldn't understand, much less control, it was easier to just blame that one guy that didn't fit in for being a witch.<br /> <br /> Blaming it all on one book or just treating witch hysteria as though it spawned ex nihilo does a disservice to the historical context that these chapters are built upon. After all, it was these religious and cultural divisions that actually <i>caused</i> the Puritans to want to set up a colony outside of England, and separate from the (Anglican) Virginia Colony. (Only to then persecute each other as soon as they were on their own, and fragment further and further until towns were primed to tear themselves apart.)<br /> <br /> To go further, I don't think you can really talk about the Puritans without also talking at least a little about English Civil War that broke out as a direct consequence of the Protestant Reformation, Splitting of the Church of England, and the various conservative and radical religious groups that fought for control of England that would lead to a Puritan movement being oppressed in England itself in the first place. Puritan fundamentalism is a direct rejection of the more materialist and conservative stance many, especially of the landed gentry wished to see enshrined in the new Church of England, since the status quo ensured their continued wealth and power. It informs their hatred of displays of wealth, gatherings for purposes of entertainment, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","user":"Wraith_Magus","date":". 02-24-2015, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T21:37:41-08:00","id":416141,"title":"","content":"The section makes it very clear it was the context of the time of CHANGE that led to the Witch Panic. Not one word of the text blames Protestant theology (other than the very specific Calvinism in play in Salem) or takes a theological position on the Reformation at all. You're inventing criticism where there isn't any.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-23-2015, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T00:10:18-08:00","id":416242,"title":"","content":"Ok, I've been thinking about Native Hunters for the Doubting Souls era, and here are a few ideas.<br /> <br /> <br /> -Obviously Les Mysteres would exist in the region. The Algonquin concept of the Manitou fits the Mysteres quite well - as does the usage of French. This is far from a universal representation of Native hunters though.<br /> <br /> -I don't have a name yet, but the Haudenosaunee (Iroquois Confederation) should have a more institutional Hunter Conspiracy. They can trace their history back to Hiawatha uniting the five peoples, and laying down the Great Law against dark magic, cannibalism, and human sacrifice. I'm thinking this Conspiracy will wield Relics, having been in the business long before Aegis Kai Doru ever stepped foot in the Americas. Their sample relic list would of course be heavy with Iroquois cultural evocation (the thunder-blasting chert of He-no, evil-repelling False Faces, and skill-granting wampum patterns) and trophies from monsters of their lore (like the literal stone-coats of the Thunenhyarhen, or the captured and bound disembodied hand of the Oniate).<br /> <br /> Think of this group as a bit of a cross between Aegis Kai Doru (relic wielders &amp; collectors against dark sorcery) and Task Force VALKYRIE (defenders of the state... and their relics serve as the eras version of Advanced Armory in their way) - as opposed to the Manitou serving Les Mysteres.<br /> <br /> - Again I don't have a name yet, but as the Algonquin women are traditionally responsible for the disposal of the dead, I thought an all female Compact dedicated to putting the walking dead to rest would be appropriate.<br /> <br /> <br /> Together with Les Voyageurs, that's 2 Compacts and 2 Conspiracies for Native Hunters in &quot;New England&quot;... I'll tinker with a few farther afield and see what I can come up with (Choctaw Conspiracy gifted with prophetic info from the sun? Navajo &quot;singers&quot; who actively seek hozoji with the supernatural, seeking them out in an effort for harmonious coeexistence?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T00:12:35-08:00","id":416244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=387256#post387256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even then, compacts and conspiracies aren't formed around race.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but they are often formed around cultural and religious specific concepts and national groups. Hence my pitch for an Iroquois Conspiracy serving the League makes as much sense to me as Task Force VALKYRIE or the Knights of Saint George.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T00:55:39-08:00","id":416266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=416242#post416242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Obviously Les Mysteres would exist in the region. The Algonquin concept of the Manitou fits the Mysteres quite well - as does the usage of French. This is far from a universal representation of Native hunters though.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm don't dislike Les Mysteres - you can do cool things with them - but their genericness was always a mark against them in my opinion.<br /> <br /> I think that becomes a much bigger issue if they became the cannon representation of Manitou hunters for example. Christianity gets two hunters with strong ties to it's denomination, it's a bit unfair if Manitou is only represented as part of a genericness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=416242#post416242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-I don't have a name yet, but the Haudenosaunee (Iroquois Confederation) should have a more institutional Hunter Conspiracy.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't know enough about Native history culture to critique it. But from a game perspective the concept sounds good.<br /> <br /> Presumably colonists and the AKD (working independantly) destroy the Conspiracy at some point?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=416242#post416242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again I don't have a name yet, but as the Algonquin women are traditionally responsible for the disposal of the dead, I thought an all female Compact dedicated to putting the walking dead to rest would be appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div> Same comment as before: I can't comment on the history, but in the abstract it looks good. Actually, this is my favourite of the lot, the idea of basing a compact around funeral rites is very cool.<br /> <br /> Wraith_Magus I'll read your comment when I have a bit more time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T01:17:19-08:00","id":416282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=416266#post416266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm don't dislike Les Mysteres - you can do cool things with them - but their genericness was always a mark against them in my opinion.<br /> <br /> I think that becomes a much bigger issue if they became the cannon representation of Manitou hunters for example. Christianity gets two hunters with strong ties to it's denomination, it's a bit unfair if Manitou is only represented as part of a genericness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well - I get the point of what they're going for with Les Mysteres, in that any Hunter group <i><b>that lets the spirits call the shots</b></i> is going to end up being less culturally defined and be united across cultural lines by those spirits' agenda (of which fighting the Uratha is an overriding concern).<br /> <br /> <br /> I agree with you 100% that Les Mysteres should NOT be a Native American catchall! That's why I'm working on these other groups. But I do think they'd be represented, particularly amongst the more animistic cultures like the Algonquin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T09:02:16-08:00","id":416530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=416141#post416141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The section makes it very clear it was the context of the time of CHANGE that led to the Witch Panic. Not one word of the text blames Protestant theology (other than the very specific Calvinism in play in Salem) or takes a theological position on the Reformation at all. You're inventing criticism where there isn't any.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it's not.<br /> <br /> The part about the witch hunts being guided by the Cainites is clearly invented history. <br /> <br /> The part about the witch hunts causing the Protestant Reformation is simply stated as though it were the agreed-upon historical fact, like how the splitting of the Church of England from Catholicism with the English King as leader of the church was a historic fact, a thing that needed to happen to keep the parallel WoD history line at least similar to our own. <br /> <br /> It's like if I were writing up a history in the parallel world, and said that of course the Middle Ages started when Genghis Khan sacked Rome and killed Augustus Caesar. You're utterly rewriting the course of events, not setting up a shadow conspiracy theory history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T10:23:37-08:00","id":416632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=416282#post416282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with you 100% that Les Mysteres should NOT be a Native American catchall!</div> </div> </div> </div> It's also that they shouldn't be a native American animism catch-all.<br /> <br /> While they would have Native American members, they are not in any shape or form actually a Native American conspiracy. They shouldn't be used in place of historically accurate animists. Or at least, as historically accurate as the Long Night / MM are to Protestantism / Catholicism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=416282#post416282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well - I get the point of what they're going for with Les Mysteres, in that any Hunter group <i><b>that lets the spirits call the shots</b></i> is going to end up being less culturally defined and be united across cultural lines by those spirits' agenda (of which fighting the Uratha is an overriding concern).</div> </div> </div> </div>As an aside - this is something I don't like about Les Mysterys.<br /> <br /> Having Spirits call the shots would be fine for NPCs in a Werewolf game, but it's questionable for PCs in a hunter game. Besides; they miss out on a great oppotunity, if Les Mysterys believed in the harmonious union of flesh and spirit and could convincingly argue that point to a Werewolf (not that the Werewolf would listen) they'd be great thematic foils with a built in reason for conflict with the Uratha.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T18:07:13-08:00","id":417018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=416632#post416632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having Spirits call the shots would be fine for NPCs in a Werewolf game, but it's questionable for PCs in a hunter game. Besides; they miss out on a great oppotunity, if Les Mysterys believed in the harmonious union of flesh and spirit and could convincingly argue that point to a Werewolf (not that the Werewolf would listen) they'd be great thematic foils with a built in reason for conflict with the Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say anything about them being dupes - i completely ignore that. But being true believers in the union of flesh &amp; spirit is not in anyway mutually exclusive with them being willingly guided by the spirits they revere, that's the &quot;calling the shots&quot; I'm talking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T18:08:04-08:00","id":417025,"title":"","content":"I'm now regretting putting the work I already have into Native Hunters since it looks like that will be a buyable reward tomorrow...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T00:44:44-08:00","id":417323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=417018#post417018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say anything about them being dupes - i completely ignore that. But being true believers in the union of flesh &amp; spirit is not in anyway mutually exclusive with them being willingly guided by the spirits they revere, that's the &quot;calling the shots&quot; I'm talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of feel that's the same thing because no sane and informed person would think letting spirits call the shots is a good idea. (Also harmonious merging happens between equals)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=417025#post417025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm now regretting putting the work I already have into Native Hunters since it looks like that will be a buyable reward tomorrow...</div> </div> </div> </div>Publish what you have anyway <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> it would be a shame to let it go to waste.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T01:10:31-08:00","id":417334,"title":"","content":"So, having no ability to conjugate and work with gender and plurals in Iroquois words, and thus only going touch existing proper nouns, the best name I have for the Haudenosaunee Conspiracy is &quot;Sons of Sosondowah&quot; - a legendary Hunter of Iroquois legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T03:01:51-08:00","id":417392,"title":"","content":"Research is making me less certain about the association between funerary practices and women with the Wampanoag specifically (being the major nation remaining nearest the Puritan colonists) - so until further notice I'm dropping that gender detail, and instead focusing on the Compact as a reaction to the <i><b>apocalyptic</b></i> devastation the Algonquin peoples of the region suffered from 1616-1619, with the Compact existing among the survivors with the goal of laying so many of their people to rest so they can find rebirth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T17:21:10-08:00","id":418117,"title":"","content":"There have been some new tiers added to the KS for expanding content. At this time, if you've got any questions about what those tiers entail your best bet is to ask Rich. None of the writers or devs have been assigned content while the KS is still going on, so if you're hoping to get something specific out of backing that tier, you'll have to confirm that with him. Thanks so much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T01:22:19-08:00","id":418508,"title":"","content":"So here's my own preliminary list of Hunter groups I'm using in the era...<br /> <br /> Tier 2<br /> - Brotherhood in the Night (Puritan Compact that in its New England form is mostly like an era's predecessor to the Long Night; its cousins back in England though are more Leveler/Digger oriented and look more like the Union than the Long Night)<br /> - Lightbringers (the &quot;Enlightenment&quot; in full swing back in Europe, these empiricists are straight up predecessors to Null Mysteriis)<br /> - Ordre de Saint Gabriel (knightly order loyal to the throne of the Sun King; probably Tier 3 in scale, but lacks the power of a supernatural Endowment)<br /> - Sequtt\u00f4i (Wampanog Compact dedicated to mourning those past and laying them to rest)<br /> - Scarlet Watch<br /> - Les Voyaguers<br /> <br /> Tier 3<br /> - Acheron Shipping &amp; Trading Guild<br /> - Lucifuge<br /> - Malleus Maleficarum<br /> - Les Mysteres (major upswing in members since the plague earlier this century, as more Native hunters in the region give themselves wholly over to the Spirits out of desperation)<br /> - Order of the Knights of Saint George (they're still operating in the name of the Church of England, but the instability of English governance with the Civil War, the Protectorate, the Restoration, and the Glorious Revolution means they don't answer to the crown anymore for their own protection - their majesties William &amp; Mary do not know they exist)<br /> - Sons of Sosondowah (a bit further inland than the English settlers currently extend, but the power of the Iroquois League is a great enough that they feel their presence none the less; these warriors of the Haudenosaunee fight to uphold the Great Law's principles against dark magic, human sacrifice, and cannibalism)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Aegis Kai Doru is still strongly rooted in what was once Byzantine territories, as extended further by the Coptic and Orthodox Churches. They don't yet have a strong presence in Western Europe or through that the New World at all.<br /> <br /> The Ascending Ones have some presence in Spanish and Portuguese territories into the New World (having had an Iberian presence since the days of Al-Andalus) but none yet in New England.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T01:52:59-08:00","id":418519,"title":"","content":"shouldn't the Silent Imperative and the Divine Artificer also take part in this? They show up in the book, just lack mechanics","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T08:30:55-08:00","id":426593,"title":"","content":"Just in case anyone is interested, my expansion proposal for Doubting Souls has been sent in to Rich. Here's what it said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The era that I would like to expand is Hunter\u2019s Doubting Souls so that it includes Hunters from the First Nations of that time period. I\u2019ve got four theme kicking around in my head, ranked roughly in order of priority.<br /> <br /> 1) A First Nations compact or conspiracy. Personally, I\u2019d prefer the former, but either could workable so I\u2019ll leave that up to you guys. This should have no ties to any European Nation or Tradition and completely be the product of Native American culture and agency.<br /> <br /> 2) A bit of an outline of the Native American Nations near Salam at this time, how hunters used to operate in them, and how the combination of European intrusion and Metacom\u2019s War has impacted their efforts. I had the Wampanoag and Pequot Nations pegged as being possible groups to focus on, but again, this is left to you discretion.<br /> <br /> 3) While its a bit further afield from Salam, Mi\u2019kmaq Nation does get mentioned briefly in Doubting Souls. Given that I am Canadian and my family is from Nova Scotia, I\u2019d love to see something about them in this time period and their Hunters.<br /> <br /> 4) Finally, I had (what I think is) a really cool idea for a small crossover. If there is space, I would like to include a brief bit about First Nations Prometheans. The key here is that these Prometheans have no ties whatsoever to anyone other than Native cultures, unless they have interacted with Europeans. They formed in North American, their demiurges were from the First Nation, and they understand their pilgrimages in cultural terms of those Nations rather than in the traditional alchemical terms of Europe. If possible, tying these Prometheans to the Mi\u2019qmak would be appreciated. I think this could survive with a paragraph to a half-page, so it may be sidebar material, but if you think there\u2019s something worth expanding and everything else is knocked off, go for it!<br /> <br /> I pretty sure that this is more than 5000 words worth of ideas there, hence the prioritization. The big thing for me here is taking the opportunity to recognize the long histories and traditions of the people who\u2019s land we live on, and have their cultural mark be left on the World Darkness in a way that honours their history. I know that your team is up to the task and that the outcome will be awesome! </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T13:35:07-07:00","id":476247,"title":"","content":"Soooo... And word on how the expansion is going? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T07:58:11-07:00","id":480234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=476247#post476247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooo... And word on how the expansion is going? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We're researching and writing. We had some really informative discussions with some gamer friends of ours who happen to have First Nations heritage and they've agreed to read over the material and offer us some insights. We've also been doing a little more playtesting of the entire chapter/material as we dive back into writing.<br /> <br /> -MMM","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Owner/Editor - FlamesRising.com","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T08:47:37-07:00","id":480277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt-M-McElroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=480234#post480234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're researching and writing. We had some really informative discussions with some gamer friends of ours who happen to have First Nations heritage and they've agreed to read over the material and offer us some insights. We've also been doing a little more playtesting of the entire chapter/material as we dive back into writing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? We need to chat soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T16:43:43-08:00","id":809205,"title":"","content":"Okay, so threadromancy time (and I figure Monica &amp; Matt may be interested in this too). <br /> <br /> One of the Native American groups that is mentioned in Doubting Souls are the Mi'kmaq. The University of Cape Breton happens to be within their traditional territory, and as par for the course for Canadian Universities, that means they offer Aboriginal Studies courses about them. <a href=\"http://www.cbu.ca/aboriginal-affairs/unamaki-college/mikm-2701/\" target=\"_blank\">MIKM 2701</a> is a little bit different since in the spirit of the Truth and Reconciliation Commission it is being offered for free, being live streamed online, and recordings of all of the lectures are being posted online. If you are looking to include First Nations in your Doubting Souls game, this could be very, very useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 01-15-2016, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T09:07:03-08:00","id":809629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=809205#post809205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so threadromancy time (and I figure Monica &amp; Matt may be interested in this too).<br /> <br /> One of the Native American groups that is mentioned in Doubting Souls are the Mi'kmaq. The University of Cape Breton happens to be within there traditional territory, and as par for the course for Canadian Universities, that means they offer Aboriginal Studies courses about them. <a href=\"http://www.cbu.ca/aboriginal-affairs/unamaki-college/mikm-2701/\" target=\"_blank\">MIKM 2701</a> is a little bit different since in the spirit of the Truth and Reconciliation Commission it is being offered for free, being live streamed online, and recordings of all of the lectures are being posted online. If you are looking to include First Nations in your Doubting Souls game, this could be very, very useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Dark Eras is in layout, but the references are always useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T05:16:40-08:00","id":828734,"title":"","content":"Needed to share with you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/bJ5t1pf.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T06:06:05-08:00","id":839097,"title":"","content":"Any idea when it will be done/printed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11379-mrimperator","name":"MrImperator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T15:56:55-08:00","id":839490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrImperator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/385184-dark-eras-hunter-chapter-doubting-souls?p=839097#post839097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any idea when it will be done/printed?</div> </div> </div> </div>When its done. I`m not trying to be flippant, but that`s all we know. Its getting closer each week. We just have to tough it out, since OP doesn`t do hard deadlines in order to improve their product quality. I think it works quite nicely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href